From: pocknix <pocknix@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: vtdr6130-cog: add the missing F0 byte to the page-select command

The vendor page switch before the B1 write is sent as "AA 10" instead of
"F0 AA 10", so the panel ignores it and B1 lands on the wrong page. Matches
the Android init sequence. Fix by Jacob Pyke and spycat88 in armada-packages
0104a (armada-os/armada#327), carried by ROCKNIX SM8250 patch 0105.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-visionox-vtdr6130-cog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-visionox-vtdr6130-cog.c
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
 					0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00);
 	}
 
-	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xAA, 0x10);
+	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xF0, 0xAA, 0x10);
 
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xB1, 
 				0x02, 0x16, 0x00, 0x14, 0x00, 0x1C, 0x00, 0x02,
